# REGRESSION -- Track B3 (D31-uniform, indirect call sigil gate): the ARRAY-
# ELEMENT cell of the callable-shape axis. When the callee expression is an
# index into a `Vector[Callable[void(int &)]]` (i.e. `arr[0]`), a bare argument
# at the invocation must REJECT at `gg check` with `E_OwnershipMismatch` --
# same rule, non-Identifier callee shape.
#
# AXIS / CELL:
#   Vector-element callee  x  bare arg vs `&`-declared param
# This is the exemplary NON-IDENTIFIER callee: the check must fire on any
# expression whose type resolves to a callable, not merely on bare-name
# callees. The prototype records `expr_types[callee.span]` at `Expr::Call`
# entry so the safety pass reaches the callable's `param_ownerships` even
# when the callee is a subscript / field-access / IIFE.
#
# Pre-B3 (RED-verified at HEAD 1028972f): `gg check` accepted the shape; the
# runtime SEGV is masked by an independent Vector-of-Callable storage/dispatch
# defect (H1 cell -- SEGV even with the correctly-sigil-spelled call). This
# fixture guards ONLY the check-time reject; the H1 storage defect is filed
# separately (`sound_callable_amp_arr_indexed_callee_segv`).
# Post-B3: `gg check` REJECTS at the argument span.
void bump(int &n):
    n = n + 100

void main():
    int a = 1
    Vector[Callable[void(int &)]] arr = [bump]
    # THE ASSERTION: bare `arr[0](a)` REJECTS -- the callable's declared param
    # is `&int`; the caller must re-spell `arr[0](&a)`.
    arr[0](a)
    print(a)
